course: dictionary
lesson: 9587
title: Streamline: smooth, simple, quick
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To streamline something means to give it a smooth, slim shape so it slips easily through air or water. It can also mean to make a job or a system simpler and quicker by removing steps that are not needed. Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning.
explain: «The racing car has a streamlined body.» The clues are racing and body. A racing car must cut through the air fast, so streamlined means smooth and slim, shaped to move easily.
explain: «We will streamline the process so each form is checked once.» The clues are process and checked once. Here streamline means make the steps simpler and quicker, not change the shape of anything.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "We will make the process simpler and quicker" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: To streamline means to make something smooth and slim, or to make a job or system simpler and quicker.
fact: «Streamlined» is the adjective: a streamlined shape moves through air or water with less resistance.
fact: Air resistance and water resistance (drag) slow moving things down, so fish, birds, racing cars and rockets are streamlined.
fact: «Streamline the process» means make the steps easier and faster by removing ones that are not needed.
fact: In science, a streamline is a line showing the path air or water takes as it flows around something.
exercise: «The racing car has a streamlined body.» What does streamlined suggest? | *Smooth and slim, so it moves easily through air | Painted in bright colours | Heavy, with lots of bumps and corners | Made of soft wood
exercise: A manager says, «We will streamline the process.» What does this mean? | Stop the process forever | *Make the steps simpler and quicker | Add more steps to check each one | Make the steps longer and harder
exercise: Which thing is streamlined so that it moves easily through water? | A pile of sand | A brick | *A fish | A flat, square box
test: «Fish and birds are streamlined.» Why are they streamlined? | So they can stay still for longer | So they are easier to see | So they become heavier | *So they can move easily through water or air
test: In science, what is a streamline? | A short line with no meaning | A line that shows how old a rock is | *A line showing the path air or water takes as it flows around something | A line drawn to measure the length of a ruler
exam: Which sentence uses «streamline» to mean make simpler and quicker? | The team will fold the form into a paper boat | The team will paint the form bright green | The team will lose the form in the bin | *The team will streamline the form so it takes less time
